+// The part of that window the slider is actually *drawn* in, measured from its
+// right hand edge: the groove, the handle that runs in it, and the few pixels
+// of rail either side.
+//
+// The window is 164 wide because the label boxes hang off to the left of the
+// groove and need the room; the track itself lives in the last forty of it.
+// Anything positioning itself beside the slider wants this number rather than
+// the window width - keeping clear of the track is what stops it swallowing the
+// drag, and keeping clear of the whole window costs a hundred points of canvas
+// for the sake of two labels that are only drawn where the handles are.
+//
+// Derived from the same terms vertical_slider() builds groove_start from, in
+// the same order, so the two cannot drift apart: the one-layer margin, half the
+// half-size one-layer button, half the groove, and the six-pixel rail border
+// the handle radius also reaches.
+float IMSlider::vertical_slider_track_width()
+{
+    return ONE_LAYER_MARGIN.x + ONE_LAYER_BUTTON_SIZE.x * 0.25f + GROOVE_WIDTH * 0.5f + 6.0f;
+}
